<title>USA: U.S. corn weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. corn weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA corn export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 1,285,400 MT--the largest since the marketing-year began--were 2 percent above the week earlier and four-fifths above the 4-week average.</p>
<p>Major increases were recorded for Taiwan (473,200 MT), Japan (428,900 MT), Mexico (60,800 MT), Indonesia (60,500 MT), and South Korea (53,900 MT).  Exports of 1,093,200 MT were 18 percent below the prior week, but 3 percent over the 4-week average.  Japan (567,700 MT) was the leading destination, followed by Colombia (98,800 MT), Taiwan (84,000 MT), and Indonesia (60,500 MT).</p>
</text>
